{
  "_comment": "Every command, route and tool name the six legacy surfaces expose on the wire, with their option and parameter names and defaults, at commit cf87774 \u2014 the last state in which all six hand-written surfaces are intact. Generated once by parsing the source, never by importing it: an import-time registry is exactly the thing Phase 2 replaces, and a fixture derived from it would move whenever it moves. premerge_public_api.json freezes Python identifiers, which say nothing about what a user can call; a CLI command, a REST path and an MCP tool name are the product's actual contract, and all six surfaces are about to be regenerated by a projector. Scope is names and defaults: CLI positional arguments are not options and are not frozen here, and response shapes are nobody's contract yet. Defaults appear as data where they are data, as source text where they are an expression, and as \"<required>\" where the parameter has no default at all. Deleting an entry from this file to make the gate pass is the one thing that defeats it.",
